{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat run-vibe.sh README.md agent.sb vibe/config.toml logs/last-run.out logs/last-run.err; git status --short; command -v sandbox-exec; command -v vibe'","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# run-vibe.sh \"<prompt>\" [workdir]: one headless Mistral Vibe run on Devstral 2 through OpenRouter, inside agent.sb.\n# The agent gets an empty scratch HOME and VIBE_HOME and only the environment names listed below (env -i), so none of\n# my other secrets reach it. OPENROUTER_API_KEY must be set in the calling shell.\nset -u\nD=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nPROMPT=$1; W=${2:-$PWD}\nREAL=\"$HOME\"\nVIBE=\"${VIBE:-$REAL/.local/bin/vibe}\"\n[ -n \"${OPENROUTER_API_KEY:-}\" ] || { echo \"set OPENROUTER_API_KEY first\"; exit 1; }\nSH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/vhome-XXXXXX); VH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/vibehome-XXXXXX)\ncp \"$D/vibe/config.toml\" \"$VH/config.toml\"\nmkdir -p \"$D/logs\"\n( cd \"$W\" && env -i PATH=\"$PATH\" TERM=\"${TERM:-dumb}\" LANG=\"${LANG:-en_US.UTF-8}\" HOME=\"$SH\" VIBE_HOME=\"$VH\" \\\n    OPENROUTER_API_KEY=\"$OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n    sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/agent.sb\" \\\n    \"$VIBE\" -p \"$PROMPT\" --model devstral --auto-approve --trust --output streaming --output-dir \"$VH/out\" \\\n      --max-price 1.5 --time-limit 1200 < /dev/null > \"$D/logs/last-run.out\" 2> \"$D/logs/last-run.err\" )\nrc=$?\n[ -d \"$VH/out\" ] && cp -R \"$VH/out\" \"$D/logs/last-run-export\"\nchmod -R u+w \"$SH\" \"$VH\" 2>/dev/null; rm -rf \"$SH\" \"$VH\"\necho \"exit $rc\"; exit $rc\n# headless Vibe runs (my setup)\n\nI run Mistral Vibe CLI 3.1.0 headless on Devstral 2 through OpenRouter, for batch coding tasks. Each run goes\nthrough `run-vibe.sh`, which starts Vibe inside a macOS sandbox (`agent.sb`) with an empty scratch HOME and an\nallowlisted environment, because the agent has a real shell and everything it sees goes to OpenRouter.\n\n- `run-vibe.sh \"<prompt>\" [workdir]`: one run; `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` comes from my shell (it is set, and it works\n  with curl against OpenRouter).\n- `agent.sb`: the sandbox. It must keep the agent away from my home folder and the Keychain; that is the whole point.\n- `vibe/config.toml`: the Vibe config (OpenRouter provider, Devstral 2).\n- `logs/last-run.out`, `logs/last-run.err`: the last run (`./run-vibe.sh \"say hi\" /tmp/x`, printed `exit 2`).\n\nEvery run ends within a second or two with exit 2 and does nothing; no export folder is written.\n;; macOS sandbox for the headless agent: it has a real shell and everything it prints goes to OpenRouter and the\n;; model host, so my real home (and the Keychain) must stay unreachable. The only things read from the home are\n;; Vibe's own install (pipx venv and its launcher). Network stays open. HOME is passed with -D.\n(version 1)\n(allow default)\n(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(deny file-write* (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(allow file-read-data (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.local/pipx\")))\n(allow file-read-data (literal (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.local/bin/vibe\")))\n(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\n# Vibe config for the headless runs: Devstral 2 (mistralai/devstral-2512) through OpenRouter, in Mistral's own\n# agent, Vibe CLI 3.1.0. Everything that would talk to Mistral's own services is off (telemetry, updates, connectors).\nactive_model = \"devstral\"\nenable_telemetry = false\nenable_update_checks = false\nenable_auto_update = false\nenable_notifications = false\nenable_connectors = false\nenable_mcp = false\nshow_greeting = false\noutside_workdir = \"deny\"\n\n[[providers]]\nname = \"openrouter\"\napi_base = \"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\"\napi_key_env_var = \"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\"\napi_style = \"openai\"\nbackend = \"generic\"\n\n[models.devstral]\nname = \"mistralai/devstral-2512\"\nprovider = \"openrouter\"\nalias = \"devstral\"\ntemperature = 0.2\ninput_price = 0.4\noutput_price = 2.0\nmax_context_length = 262144\nReading API keys from the macOS Keychain (set them as environment variables to skip this)\nError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted: '/usr/bin/security'\n/usr/bin/sandbox-exec\n/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.local/bin/vibe\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The saved error shows Vibe trying to run `/usr/bin/security` to read the Keychain, which the sandbox correctly blocks. I’m checking why the supplied API key and config are not preventing that lookup."}}
